<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guadalupe Victoria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1786">1786</a>–<a href="/years/1843">1843</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as José Miguel Fernández y Félix</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guadalupe Victoria, born José Miguel Fernández y Félix, was a general of the Mexican War of Independence and the first President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, from 1824 to 1829. He took his adopted name in honour of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/our-lady-of-guadalupe">Virgin of Guadalupe</a> and of victory. His government won recognition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and began the expulsion of Spanish residents, and he was the only president to complete his term for decades.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guadalupe-victoria.jpg" alt="Guadalupe Victoria" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlos Paris · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guadalupe_Victoria_-_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
